            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12968/hmed.2016.77.1.24</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Laparoscopic surgery has become increasingly common with reduced postoperative pain and faster recovery. Clinicians managing patients undergoing abdominal laparoscopic surgery should appreciate the physiological changes which mainly arise from patient positioning and the effects of pneumoperitoneum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
